> > with the exception of the X, there was no way to know where any of
> > this stuff came from.
> 
> That's when it was legal.  Street "MDMA" now is apparently really bad.

The stuff we got seemed to be the same chemical each time but varied
wildly in strength. Some of it was purportedly "time release" and this
was much better. One frightening thing about X is that in, wild guess,
one trip out of six, there is a "mini-rush" that feels like total
paralysis and terror and makes people think that they are about to
have a miserable time. I saw it happen to friends twice and it
happened to me once. Lasted one minute, fifty seconds. A LONG time
when you can't breathe! Trip was fine after that; the relief was
multiplied by the drug.
  The most impressive thing about X, to me, was that it allowed two
people to communicate to the point nearly of telepathy. I took it with
a roommate with whom I was not that close, and we ended up swapping
life stories, in a bed, with no clothes on and no sexual contact or
feelings, for about six hours, and the insights we gained into our 
relationship were permanent and "real." (X's reputation as an
aphrodisiac, IMHO, is overrated; like speed, you can go longer but
with less gain.) Had a similar experience with another friend, and
again, the breaking down of barriers was permanent. We used to talk
about getting Reagan and Gorbachev (sp?) alone in a room with it. It's
a chemically-induced state of trust and openness that is, well, hard
to imagine achieving under normal circumstances.
  The drug was ROUGH on the system though; I felt burnt out for
several days each time. We heard rumors about nutritional
countermeasures but I never took it enough to investigate...the fear
of damage outweighed the risk to me. I think I'd take it with my SO if
a) we could get the real thing and b) we hadn't both sworn off all
drugs a long time ago. 

About the pot and mescaline: a couple of people have told me mescaline
isn't a reasonable thing to find in pot. That was a wild guess... we
got one batch that made colors look bright and LSD-style but oddly
geometric visual disturbances.

  The main reason I gave up pot was that the drug changed too much. The
pot I smoked in high school compared to the pot I got after college
was like red wine compared to cheap whiskey. When I started, we got
this mild, gray, mexican pot that was light and relaxing and gave us
the giggles and cost $15/ounce. On rare occasions someone would
produce sensimilla that was strong and erotic. The "Columbian" we
started seeing in the early 80's would reduce me to a tense, immobile
zombie incapable of motion or humor. I know that the active
ingredient in pot is a family of chemicals, and I suspect that it has
been bred to be stronger; possibly I react badly to the new mix, or
possibly it takes more to make people numb these days!

  Footnote: a couple of years ago I befriended someone who still
smokes pot and I gave it another taste. He was paying $50 for a
quarter ounce, and it was numbingly strong. Ten years of added social
skills allowed men to be a bit more social through the haze, but I
found it a very unpleasant experience still, and I feel no desire to
try it again.

To get back to an Extropian theme, I'm sure that if we had a free
market, someone would be selling the "light" pot of my youth...
"tastes great, less chilling!"



